in this video i'm going to be breaking  down the second episode  of attack on titan season 4. unlike the  first episode  this one was less focused on action and  it was more about the characters  strategizing what they need to do next  so in this video i'll explain everything  that i thought was interesting  including zeke's plan falco's feelings  and a bunch of other stuff that you  might have missed  be sure to hit that sub button if you  want to see more attack on titan videos  like this  and of course let me know what you  thought of the episode down below  okay so episode two was called midnight  train and it starts off with the mali  generals  discussing the aftermath of the war we  saw last week  i know some people were really confused  about what that war was about  so to summarize it quickly the battle in  the last episode was the culmination of  a four-year war  that the nation of mali was involved in  mali is where characters like zeke and  reiner are from  and this four-year war started because  other nations thought that mali was  vulnerable  after losing the colossal titan and the  female titan  that's why in the first episode zeke  said it was their failure that caused  the war to happen in the first place  coming back to episode 2 the mali  generals have begun to realize  that technology is beginning to surpass  the power of the titans  i mean we saw it even though they won  the war the anti-titan weaponry that  their enemies have developed  is a sign that titans won't be enough to  win future wars  all this talking culminated in maz  mickelson realizing  that other nations are surpassing mali  when it comes to technology  and something needs to be done this is  where zeke's plan comes in  because he believes that if they were to  invade paradise island again  and reclaim all the titans then this  would give marley enough time to safely  develop technology that would you know  bring them back up to speed with the  other nations  as the beast titan zeke only has one  year left to live due to the curse of  ymir  and so he wants to invade the island as  soon as possible  zeke's successor is colt grice and if  everything goes to plan  then he will be the one to inherit the  beast titan in a year's time  moving on episode 2 gives us a look into  reiner's mindset  as he is still traumatized from the  events that happened on the island  he's grilled by porco galliard who is  the new draw titan  and i did a video about poco's backstory  if you're interested  poco believes that ryan never should  have been sent to the island in the  first place  and he just absolutely roasts him for  all his failures  including the fact that pogo's brother  died to save reiner whilst they were on  the island  later in the episode we get another look  at the four new warrior candidates  and one of these guys will be the next  person to inherit the armored titan  reiner later admits in the episode that  gabby is the one who will most likely  get it  but in truth falco wants the armor titan  just as badly  for reasons we'll get to in a minute an  interesting thing to note about this  episode  is that with the titans becoming less  useful in war  this means that the usefulness of the  aldean race has  also decreased as we found out in season  3  eldians are the only type of human that  can transform into a titan  and because of this they suffer from  racism all over the world  tamale the main usefulness of eldians is  that they can become  titan shifters but as one of the warrior  candidates mentioned  what will happen to them once the titans  are obsolete  it's possible that eldians could be  exterminated or maybe treated even worse  than they currently are  anyway moving back to the reason that  falco wants to inherit the armored titan  he revealed in this episode that he  essentially wants to get it  so that he can save gabby's life if gabi  was to get the armored titan  then she'd be guaranteed to die within  13 years due to the curse of ymir  not to mention the fact that she'd  probably die even sooner than that  because anti-titan technology keeps  improving because falco clearly has a  crush on her  he wants her to live and reina tells him  that if he wants to inherit the armor  then his only option is to surpass gabby  and become  a better warrior than she is as the  episode progresses  the train takes the aldians back to  liberio which is the hometown that  reiner kept referring to during the  earlier seasons  liberia is a malian city which has a  segregated area for aldeans to live  which is just further evidence of the  discrimination that they face  in liberio eldians have to wear armbands  to signify their status  warrior candidates like falco have  yellow armbands and titan shifters such  as reiner  wear red armbands including their family  as well these red armbands give them  pretty high status when it comes to  aldians  but they still have to live inside the  segregated zone  as falco is on his way home he notices a  bunch of eldian soldiers on their way  to be treated at the hospital we saw in  episode 1 how eldians during war  are basically expected to give their  lives for no reason  and commander mcgath was originally  going to sacrifice 800 aldeans  before gabby decided to step in with her  plan which is why everyone was praising  her during the episode  anyway falco notices how one of the  aldian soldiers  has his armband on his right arm which  is not something a person from liberia  would normally do  because it's always meant to be on the  left falco helps this person put the  armband on the other side  and tells the man that he doesn't need  to fight any longer this man has very  interesting features  but i will leave that to your  imagination this moment was then  followed by  family dinner in the brawn household and  i should probably mention that gabby and  reina are cousins which is why they're  having dinner together  what was interesting about this scene  was the difference in mentality  between rhino and the rest of his family  as someone who's actually been to the  island  reiner knows in his heart that eldians  on the island are just like normal  people  whereas gabby and his mother and the  rest of his family  they're convinced that the island must  be full of devils that need to be  exterminated  reiner himself used to believe this but  now that he knows the truth about the  island  everything's kind of changed and gabby  is beginning to notice the difference  in rhino's personality episode 2 ends  with the warriors of mali having a  meeting  and the anime left out this wonderful  scene of pete crawling on all fours  which i will personally never forgive  them for as the cart titan she stays on  all fours for long periods of time  so it's just started to feel more  natural for her to be in this position  which is why she was lying down during  the meeting and why she had a crutch at  the beginning of the episode  zeke explains to the warriors that when  technology you know when it's  finally a hundred percent surpass the  titans then eldians are finished  he explains his plan to invade the  island and retake the founding titan  which will give mali enough time to  rebuild their military  however even if the plan is successful  it won't actually do anything to stop  aliens being persecuted this is when  zeke unveils an additional plan to save  the eldian race  which requires the help of the tiber  family the type of family are the  holders of the warhammer titan  which is the only titan not yet seen in  the anime they are the most respected  aldeans on the planet  as their ancestors are widely known to  have fought against the aldian royal  family  during the great titan war the great  titan war is what resulted  in mali gaining the power of virtually  every titan shifter  except obviously the founding titan and  the attack titan not only are the tibers  incredibly wealthy  but they don't interfere with the lives  of regular ldm people  this is why eldians live in the  segregated zones as the tigers just  choose not to get involved  zeke announces that the tigers are  finally ready to help out  and will use their position to remind  the world of the threat the island poses  and in doing so they will kind of like  make it seem  that mali will invade the island very  soon this strategy is designed to show  the world  that the good elden warriors are going  to stop the bad eldians who live on the  island  which will hopefully go a long way to  stopping discrimination against their  kind  as this meeting took place mali and  generals were secretly listening in the  other room  to see if all the warriors were showing  any signs of dissent  zeke subtly warned the group that they  were being listened to but it seems that  rhino was the only one who noticed  and that's why during the episode reiner  interrupted porco  because he didn't want poker to say  anything that was incriminating  but anyway guys that was the breakdown  for episode 2 of attack on titan season  4.  i'd appreciate if you dropped a like if  you liked it and be sure to check out  this other video i did  which imagined which my hero academia  characters would inherit the nine titan  shifters  until the next one peace out

